  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Origin coordinates; destination owns execution",
      "items": [
        "Remote requests use verified embedded Go SSH to the selected installed Delegate. The prepared destination validates root/task identity and calls the same task lifecycle shown here (internal/app/remote_exchange.go:17–39; remote_serve.go:77–99,207–258).",
        "A persistent destination supervisor must already be ready. The destination owns admission, budgets, cancellation, native closure and outcome.json. An SSH disconnect changes connectivity, not the task verdict (internal/app/remote_owner.go:41–55; remote_serve.go:272–284).",
        "The origin stores immutable intent, acceptance and dated observations. After an uncertain send, recovery reconciles the existing request; it never authorizes a second admission. Downloaded declared outputs and caches do not replace the destination outcome (internal/remote/coordinator.go:24–103,166–173).",
        "Local Teams, schedules and managed Git capture remain optional local paths. Remote references do not support logs or continuation; provider installations, accounts and configuration remain destination-owned (internal/app/remote_cli.go:294–321)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Saved is not running",
      "items": [
        "Start plain delegate scheduler serve in an independent user terminal or tmux pane, even before the first definition. Agent and manual commands omit --root and share that OS-default store from any project cwd; each schedule retains its workspace. Saving never starts a host.",
        "The host supervises/restarts its resident child. The child runs the calendar loop; GoCron only offers wake hints, with no definition or claim authority (internal/scheduler/pulse/source.go:18–54).",
        "Explicit serve and schedule create share the absent-storage initializer. An empty calendar can be ready; passive reads and compatibility scheduler run never initialize storage. Existing custom roots remain available with their exact --root."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Recovery and stopping",
      "items": [
        "A retryable child exit recovers with backoff while the host lives. Host/pane loss or reboot needs manual start again; permanent host faults stop retries (internal/scheduler/host/lifecycle.go:61–113).",
        "Downtime becomes compact skipped history, with no catch-up backlog. Active or uncertain occurrences block overlap (internal/scheduler/runtime/decision.go:26–69).",
        "Stop acceptance is not completed shutdown. Wait for host/child closure; already admitted independent workers continue under their own supervisors and budgets (internal/scheduler/host/lifecycle.go:116–190; internal/scheduler/runtime/loop.go:41–45)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Team defaults and recorded context",
      "items": [
        "Team commands mutate the separate catalog (internal/app/teams_commands.go:114–133). New Team-targeted tasks resolve current Member defaults before admission; caller choices stay authoritative. Roles describe work and grant no permissions.",
        "Each new scheduled occurrence resolves current defaults. Same-task replay uses recorded selection; continuation inherits recorded Team context and config under explicit caller override rules (internal/app/teams_schedule_create.go:25–51; internal/tasklifecycle/continuation_request.go:9–26).",
        "Calendar dispatch calls the existing lifecycle in process only after a definitely new committed claim. Existing claims or uncertain readback do not authorize another invocation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One task path and result owner",
      "items": [
        "Pueue queues worker starts, not calendar recurrence. The guardian owns the task lifetime; delegate-run performs fresh preflight, starts the selected provider and captures output. Receipt precedes enqueue; closure precedes sealing and publication.",
        "TaskDir evaluates sealed evidence and commits outcome.json. Status, logs and collect observe that task; collection can reconcile saved evidence without launching a provider turn (internal/tasklifecycle/collection.go:13–63).",
        "Confirmed pressure refuses fresh admission before ordinary task-record creation; unavailable metrics alone warn. The public response can still be unknown for a caller-supplied ID: follow its next_action, never infer absence or replay (internal/tasklifecycle/dispatch.go:17–48; resource_admission.go:119–151)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Optional workspace capture",
      "items": [
        "Managed Git isolation adds a checkout and capture receipts. Capture stays independent of the provider task outcome and requires its helper lifetime to close.",
        "Workspace helpers reuse the supervised task path. The lead reviews the capture and explicitly releases the retained checkout. Provider installations, settings and accounts stay user/provider-owned."
      ]
    }
  ]
